Description: Selected fixes from upstream "Fixes (#275)" (813ca0d) and ad44d84
 Backports the correctness- and security-relevant parts of upstream
 commit 813ca0d ("Fixes (#275)", Doug Nazar) plus the ssl_verify_callback
 logging fix from ad44d84 ("Improve error responses"). Notably:
 .
 * acl.c: the netmask computation used '-1 << (32 - prefix)', which is
   undefined behaviour; for prefix 0 (e.g. "0.0.0.0/0" in allowed_hosts)
   it actually evaluated to a /32 mask on common platforms, silently
   denying every host. Now uses an explicit zero mask for /0 and
   '~0u <<' otherwise.
 * acl.c/acl.h: clear_allowed_hosts() frees the ACL lists before
   (re)parsing allowed_hosts. Previously every SIGHUP reload or
   additional allowed_hosts line appended to the existing lists, so
   hosts removed from the configuration kept their access.
   The head pointers were also moved from a header (where 'static' gave
   every translation unit its own copy) into acl.c.
 * acl.c: is_an_allowed_host() debug output used inet_ntoa() twice in
   one call, printing the same address twice (static buffer).
 * nrpe.c: my_system() read() output into a buffer that was passed to
   strncat() without NUL termination - a stack over-read when plugin
   output chunks contain no NUL byte. The buffer is now terminated
   after every read.
 * nrpe.c: process_metachars() loop condition used the comma operator
   ('i < length, j < length'), which discards the i-check.
 * nrpe.c: config options re-assigned with strdup() now free() the old
   value first (leaks on duplicate lines and SIGHUP reloads).
 * nrpe.c: read_config_dir() now checks the snprintf() return value for
   truncation instead of silently using a cut-off path.
 * nrpe.c: the connection fd_set is only reallocated when it needs to
   grow and is freed on shutdown (valgrind leak).
 * nrpe.c/utils.c: asprintf() return values are checked instead of
   relying on the output pointer being NULL on failure.
 * nrpe-ssl.c: the SSL verify callback now also logs certificate details
   for certificates that verify OK when SSL_LogCertDetails is requested
   (was: '||' short-circuit, so details were only printed for failures).
 .
 The full my_system() rewrite from 813ca0d (splitting parent/child IO
 loops) is intentionally not included; the truncation/over-read was
 fixed surgically and the non-blocking pipe already prevents deadlock.
